## Context

`src/aedist/plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.py` hand-types "§2" in four places
(lines ~27, ~199, ~280, and the figure annotation at ~424), but the quality bar
is defined in §3 of `slides/manuscript/main.md` ("Quality dimensions for
research-grade statistical datasets"). The §2 label is therefore **wrong**, and
because line 424 is a matplotlib annotation, the stale number is rendered
*inside* `report/inputs/generated/fig_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.pdf` — visible
in the built manuscript PDF as "dark red ⇒ the §2 quality bar is not cleared".

This is the same defect class ticket 0518 removed from the manuscript prose
(hand-typed cross-reference numbers that drift), but living in a `plot_*.py`
annotation that the manuscript's pandoc-crossref machinery cannot reach. Found
during the 0518 migration; pre-existing on origin/main, out of 0518's scope.

## Relevant files
- `src/aedist/plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.py` — four "§2" occurrences;
  line ~424 is the figure-internal annotation that renders into the PDF.
- `report/inputs/generated/fig_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.pdf` — regenerated
  artifact carrying the stale label.

## Actions
1. Decide the policy for section references inside figure annotations: a plot
   script has no access to pandoc-crossref's numbering. Either (a) drop the
   "§N" entirely from the annotation (e.g. "the quality bar is not cleared"),
   or (b) refer to it by name ("the four-dimensional quality bar") so no number
   is hand-typed. Option (b) is preferred — names don't drift.
2. Apply the same fix to the three docstring/comment occurrences for accuracy.
3. Regenerate the figure (`make -f experiments/render.mk …`) and confirm the
   rendered annotation no longer carries a section number.

## Test
- An adherence test asserting `plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.py` contains no
  hand-typed `§\d` literal (the figure-annotation analogue of
  `tests/test_manuscript_crossref.py`).

## Verification
- [ ] No `§\d` literal remains in the plot script.
- [ ] Regenerated heatmap PDF annotation carries no section number.
- [ ] `make check` green.

## Exit criteria
- The stale/hardcoded section reference is removed from the plot script and its
  regenerated figure; a guard prevents regression.

## Related
Surfaced during the 0518 symbolic-cross-reference migration.
